# KIT Consulting Website - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is the official website for KIT Consulting, an engineering consultancy specializing in construction execution, tendering, and process optimization.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15.1.2 with App Router
- React 18.3.1
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS v4.1.9
- shadcn/ui components (full library)
- Magic UI components (add as needed from magicui.design)
- Framer Motion for animations
- Lucide React for icons
- Deployed on Vercel

## Code Style & Conventions

### TypeScript
- Use strict TypeScript with proper type definitions
- Define interfaces in `lib/types.ts`
- Use type imports: `import type { Type } from '...'`
- Avoid `any` types

### React & Next.js
- Use Server Components by default
- Add `"use client"` only when necessary (forms, state, interactivity)
- Use async/await for Server Components
- Follow Next.js 15 conventions (await params, searchParams, etc.)

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Follow the brand color palette:
  - Primary: #003366
  - Secondary: #0066cc
  - Accent: #e5e5e5
- Use semantic color tokens from globals.css
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Use `leading-relaxed` for body text
- Use `text-balance` or `text-pretty` for headings

### Component Structure
- Keep components small and focused
- Use composition over large components
- Place reusable components in `/components`
- Page-specific components can stay in page files

### File Naming
- Use kebab-case for files: `contact-form.tsx`
- Use PascalCase for components: `ContactForm`
- Use camelCase for utilities and functions

### Data Management
- Static data in `lib/data/` as JSON files
- Type definitions in `lib/types.ts`
- Use Server Components to fetch data when possible

## Brand Guidelines

### Colors
- Primary Blue: #003366 (headers, primary elements)
- Secondary Blue: #0066cc (links, CTAs, accents)
- White: #FFFFFF (backgrounds)
- Gray: #666666 (body text)
- Light Gray: #e5e5e5 (borders, subtle backgrounds)

### Typography
- Font: Inter (from next/font/google)
- Headings: Bold, text-[#003366]
- Body: Regular, text-[#666666], leading-relaxed
- Links: text-[#0066cc], hover:text-[#003366]

### Spacing
- Use Tailwind spacing scale (p-4, p-6, p-8, etc.)
- Consistent section padding: py-16 md:py-24
- Container: container-custom class (max-width: 1280px)

## API Routes

### Contact Form
- Endpoint: `/api/contact`
- Method: POST
- Body: `{ name, email, company, message }`
- TODO: Integrate with Zoho Mail SMTP

## Deployment

### Vercel Configuration
- Framework: Next.js
- Build Command: `npm run build`
- Output Directory: `.next`
- Install Command: `npm install`

### Environment Variables (Future)
- `ZOHO_EMAIL`: Zoho email address
- `ZOHO_PASSWORD`: Zoho app password

## Development Workflow

1. Run dev server: `npm run dev`
2. Test on multiple screen sizes
3. Check accessibility (semantic HTML, ARIA labels)
4. Validate forms and error states
5. Test all navigation links
6. Build before committing: `npm run build`

## SEO Checklist
- ✅ Metadata in all pages
- ✅ Semantic HTML structure
- ✅ Alt text for images
- ✅ sitemap.xml
- ✅ robots.txt
- ✅ Open Graph tags

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include ARIA labels where needed
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain color contrast ratios
- Test with screen readers

## Performance
- Use Next.js Image component for images
- Lazy load components when appropriate
- Minimize client-side JavaScript
- Use Server Components by default
- Optimize fonts with next/font

